<title>USA: Car rental companies stop taking debit cards - NYT.</title>
<headline>Car rental companies stop taking debit cards - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Large U.S. car rental companies have stopped letting people rent cars using just a Visa Check card or Mastercard's Master Money card, the New York Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Debit cards &quot;provide no qualification of creditworthiness,&quot; a Hertz spokeswoman was quoted as saying in the paper.</p>
<p>The paper said both Hertz and Avis had stopped letting people rent cars with such cards.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
